Subject: RE: patch for lib/Term/Cap.pm for EBCDIC platform

On Thu, 2007-10-25 at 09:05 +0200, Konovalov, Vadim Vladimirovich
(Vadim)** CTR ** wrote:
> > Here is the patch below. Any question, pls let me know, thanks.
> 
> ... and now all systems will check for 
>       if (ord("A") == 193) {
> 
> how annoying.

Why? If you are running Tgetent more than once in an application then
something weird is going on.

> 
> that file contains already:
> if ( $^O eq 'VMS') {
>        chomp (my @entry = );
>        $VMS_TERMCAP = join '', @entry;
> }
> 
> 
> is it possible to factor out EBCDIC logic in a better way?
> 

We'd still need to do runtime detection of EBDIC in a manner similar to
the above, if it became necessary to do this more than once then yes I'd
agree but as it stands it'll be fine  and I'm going to leave it as it
is.

> moreover, your if/else lines below have very much common lines, is it necessary?

> silently duplicating all runtime lines because of EBCDIC is not good.
> 

It's only really a *maintenance* problem and I'll fix it if it annoys
me.

I'm going to tackle one of the longstanding TODO items when I've rebuilt
a FreeBSD machine and after 5.10 is out so I can address that then.


